// What repeats. A plan is a template: the journal writes an occurrence as the
// plan's name (`2025-03-05 manager-fee`), or with what differs (`2025-06-05
// manager-fee 198 USD`, `mortgage-payment` with new legs), and the forecast
// projects the rest. Each ends where its reason ends: nothing after the sale.

/// Monthly pay from the day job, before and after tax.
plan paycheck every month on 28 from 2025-01-28 income/salary -> 8_000.00 USD
  taxes/federal       1_215.00 USD
  taxes/payroll       612.00 USD
  checking            ...

/// Tenant A: 2,400 USD a month on the first, February to August.
plan rent-a every month on 1 from 2025-02-01 until 2025-08 income/rent -> rental-bank 2_400 USD #lease-a

/// Tenant B: 2,500 USD a month from October. The lease runs to 2026-09-30, but the
/// house is sold on 2025-12-29 and the buyer takes the lease: the plan stops there.
plan rent-b every month on 1 from 2025-10-01 until 2025-12 income/rent -> rental-bank 2_500 USD #lease-b

/// The mortgage payment is fixed; what goes to principal grows every month. The
/// legs below are the first payment's, and each later occurrence writes its own.
plan mortgage-payment every month on 1 from 2025-02-01 until 2025-12 rental-bank -> 1_809.59 USD / lender
  mortgage            240.21 USD for #loan   // principal
  interest            1_569.38 USD   // interest

/// Property management, 8% of the month's rent, paid the month after.
plan manager-fee every month on 5 from 2025-03-05 until 2025-12 rental-bank -> management 192 USD / hartwell-pm

/// Depreciation is a deduction with no cash: 27.5 years straight line on the
/// building (80% of the price; the land is not depreciable), a whole month at
/// 913.58 USD. The first and last months are half months (mid-month convention),
/// and the roof adds its own from September.
plan depreciation every month on 31 from 2025-01-31 until 2025-12 house.basis -> expenses/rental/depreciation 913.58 USD
